---
title: House vinaigrette
servings: 8
tags: [basics, sauce, make-ahead]
source: Invented for this repository
notes: Keeps a fortnight in the fridge. Shake before each use.
---

Put the @white wine vinegar{60%ml}, @dijon mustard{1%tsp} and a pinch of
@flaked sea salt{} into a #jam jar{} and shake until the salt has dissolved.

Add the @olive oil{180%ml} and shake hard for ~{30%seconds}, until it thickens
and stops separating immediately.

-- The ratio is three parts oil to one part vinegar. Everything else is taste.

Taste on a leaf rather than a spoon; it reads much sharper on its own.
